From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] migration: x-defer-disk-flush, no flush to the host's disk
 while the VM is stopped for a switchover

Stopping the VM for a migration's switchover drains the disks and then
flushes them (do_vm_stop): an fdatasync of every image the guest wrote
since its last flush.  On a host whose disk other writers keep busy
that fdatasync waits for them, and the guest stays stopped meanwhile.
Traced in spin-machine (a checkpoint beside four host writers on the
same ext4, the guest writing its disk with O_DIRECT, QEMU -trace on
runstate_set, vm_stop_flush_all and luring_co_submit), the time from
finish-migrate to pre-switchover was one io_uring fsync, 13-79 ms on
the bench and up to 527 ms on a laptop.  Deferred to the switchover's
end, the same fsync came back in cont: activating a qcow2 node closes
and reopens it, and the close flushes.

A migration whose reader shares this host's page cache, a checkpoint to
a file on it, needs the images' writes to reach the page cache, not the
disk: QEMU does not sync the migration file either, and whoever keeps
the checkpoint syncs both.  So add the capability x-defer-disk-flush.
With it, the stop drains the disks, then defers every flush to the
host's disk until the VM runs again (vm_prepare_start) or QEMU closes
the disks (bdrv_close_all): a flush writes back what a driver caches,
such as qcow2's metadata, to the OS and leaves the node unflushed, so
that the next flush after, the guest's or the host's, forces it.  The
deferral starts after the drain, so every flush the guest asked for
before the stop has reached the disk, and the guest can make no other
until it runs.  A seal at pre-switchover (blockdev-snapshot flushes the
node it puts under the overlay) and the activation in cont are deferred
the same way.

The stop itself decides, from its run state: do_vm_stop and
vm_stop_force_state's stopped branch start the deferral after their
drain when the state is finish-migrate and the capability holds.  The
alternative, an argument threaded through migration_stop_vm, a second
vm_stop_force_state and the stop's helpers, took about 80 more lines to
say the same.  Postcopy's and CPR's stops are finish-migrate too, and
migrate_defer_disk_flush() is false with postcopy-ram or a CPR mode:
only precopy's completion was traced and measured, and CPR's stop can
precede a host reboot (cpr-reboot), which loses what the page cache
holds.  The accessor is in migration/misc.h, the header the
rest of QEMU reads migration from.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 block.c                            |  3 +++
 block/io.c                         | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 include/block/block-global-state.h |  1 +
 include/migration/misc.h           |  1 +
 migration/options.c                | 13 +++++++++++++
 qapi/migration.json                | 13 +++++++++++--
 system/runstate.c                  | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 7 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/block.c b/block.c
index 006c34134..22b09a3eb 100644
--- a/block.c
+++ b/block.c
@@ -5266,6 +5266,9 @@ void bdrv_close_all(void)
     GLOBAL_STATE_CODE();
     assert(job_next(NULL) == NULL);
 
+    /* What a stopped VM's deferred flushes left goes to the disk now */
+    bdrv_defer_flush_to_disk(false);
+
     /* Drop references from requests still in flight, such as canceled block
      * jobs whose AIO context has not been polled yet */
     bdrv_drain_all();
diff --git a/block/io.c b/block/io.c
index 0f81b7e6b..dea789eb5 100644
--- a/block/io.c
+++ b/block/io.c
@@ -2357,6 +2357,22 @@ int coroutine_fn bdrv_co_pwrite_zeroes(BdrvChild *child, int64_t offset,
                            BDRV_REQ_ZERO_WRITE | flags);
 }
 
+static bool flush_to_disk_deferred;
+
+/*
+ * While deferred, a flush writes back what a driver caches to the OS but
+ * does not force it to the disk, and leaves the node unflushed, so that the
+ * next flush after bdrv_defer_flush_to_disk(false) forces it.  Meant for
+ * while the guest is stopped and drained, whose own flushes are then all
+ * done: what is deferred is the host's flush, not a guest's.  The guest's
+ * first flush once it runs again forces what the host's left.
+ */
+void bdrv_defer_flush_to_disk(bool defer)
+{
+    GLOBAL_STATE_CODE();
+    qatomic_set(&flush_to_disk_deferred, defer);
+}
+
 /*
  * Flush ALL BDSes regardless of if they are reachable via a BlkBackend or not.
  */
@@ -3045,6 +3061,7 @@ int coroutine_fn bdrv_co_flush(BlockDriverState *bs)
     BdrvChild *child;
     int current_gen;
     int ret = 0;
+    bool deferred = false;
     IO_CODE();
 
     assert_bdrv_graph_readable();
@@ -3092,6 +3109,11 @@ int coroutine_fn bdrv_co_flush(BlockDriverState *bs)
         goto flush_children;
     }
 
+    if (qatomic_read(&flush_to_disk_deferred)) {
+        deferred = true;
+        goto flush_children;
+    }
+
     BLKDBG_CO_EVENT(primary_child, BLKDBG_FLUSH_TO_DISK);
     if (!bs->drv) {
         /* bs->drv->bdrv_co_flush() might have ejected the BDS
@@ -3149,7 +3171,7 @@ flush_children:
 
 out:
     /* Notify any pending flushes that we have completed */
-    if (ret == 0) {
+    if (ret == 0 && !deferred) {
         bs->flushed_gen = current_gen;
     }
 
diff --git a/include/block/block-global-state.h b/include/block/block-global-state.h
index ed89999f0..48bca6649 100644
--- a/include/block/block-global-state.h
+++ b/include/block/block-global-state.h
@@ -196,6 +196,7 @@ void bdrv_activate_all(Error **errp);
 int GRAPH_UNLOCKED bdrv_inactivate_all(void);
 
 int bdrv_flush_all(void);
+void bdrv_defer_flush_to_disk(bool defer);
 void GRAPH_UNLOCKED bdrv_close_all(void);
 void GRAPH_UNLOCKED bdrv_drain_all_begin(void);
 void bdrv_drain_all_begin_nopoll(void);
diff --git a/include/migration/misc.h b/include/migration/misc.h
index 86cc7eefd..b5130a269 100644
--- a/include/migration/misc.h
+++ b/include/migration/misc.h
@@ -167,5 +167,6 @@ bool multifd_join_device_state_save_threads(void);
 void migration_request_switchover_ack_legacy(const char *requester);
 
 bool migrate_local(void);
+bool migrate_defer_disk_flush(void);
 
 #endif
diff --git a/migration/options.c b/migration/options.c
index bd40394aa..5f2f597a4 100644
--- a/migration/options.c
+++ b/migration/options.c
@@ -354,6 +354,19 @@ bool migrate_events(void)
     return s->capabilities[MIGRATION_CAPABILITY_EVENTS];
 }
 
+/*
+ * Postcopy's and CPR's stops are finish-migrate too, and never defer: only
+ * precopy's completion was measured, and CPR's stop can precede a host
+ * reboot (cpr-reboot), which loses what the page cache holds.
+ */
+bool migrate_defer_disk_flush(void)
+{
+    MigrationState *s = migrate_get_current();
+
+    return s->capabilities[MIGRATION_CAPABILITY_X_DEFER_DISK_FLUSH] &&
+           !migrate_postcopy_ram();
+}
+
 bool migrate_mapped_ram(void)
 {
     MigrationState *s = migrate_get_current();
diff --git a/qapi/migration.json b/qapi/migration.json
index 889a9b89c..592073828 100644
--- a/qapi/migration.json
+++ b/qapi/migration.json
@@ -518,9 +518,17 @@
 #     each RAM page.  Requires a migration URI that supports seeking,
 #     such as a file.  (since 9.0)
 #
+# @x-defer-disk-flush: If enabled, a precopy switchover's stop
+#     completes the guest's flushes, then leaves the disks' writes in
+#     the host's page cache until the VM runs again or QEMU closes the
+#     disks.  For a migration whose reader shares this host's page
+#     cache, such as a checkpoint to a file on it.  Ignored with
+#     @postcopy-ram or a CPR mode.  (since 11.2)
+#
 # Features:
 #
-# @unstable: Members @x-colo and @x-ignore-shared are experimental.
+# @unstable: Members @x-colo, @x-ignore-shared and
+#     @x-defer-disk-flush are experimental.
 #
 # Since: 1.2
 ##
@@ -534,7 +542,8 @@
            { 'name': 'x-ignore-shared', 'features': [ 'unstable' ] },
            'validate-uuid', 'background-snapshot',
            'zero-copy-send', 'postcopy-preempt', 'switchover-ack',
-           'dirty-limit', 'mapped-ram'] }
+           'dirty-limit', 'mapped-ram',
+           { 'name': 'x-defer-disk-flush', 'features': [ 'unstable' ] }] }
 
 ##
 # @MigrationCapabilityStatus:
diff --git a/system/runstate.c b/system/runstate.c
index 56bfc5b07..c59fdb1ef 100644
--- a/system/runstate.c
+++ b/system/runstate.c
@@ -444,6 +444,16 @@ static int do_vm_stop(RunState state, bool send_stop)
     }
 
     bdrv_drain_all();
+    /*
+     * A precopy switchover under x-defer-disk-flush defers every flush to
+     * the host's disk until the VM runs again (vm_prepare_start) or the
+     * disks are closed (bdrv_close_all).  It starts after the drain, which
+     * completed every request the guest made, so no flush of the guest's is
+     * deferred.
+     */
+    if (state == RUN_STATE_FINISH_MIGRATE && migrate_defer_disk_flush()) {
+        bdrv_defer_flush_to_disk(true);
+    }
     /*
      * Even if vm_state_notify() return failure,
      * it would be better to flush as before.
@@ -517,6 +527,11 @@ int vm_prepare_start(bool step_pending)
     /* We are sending this now, but the CPUs will be resumed shortly later */
     qapi_event_send_resume();
 
+    /*
+     * The guest runs again, and its next flush forces what the host's
+     * deferred flushes left in the page cache.
+     */
+    bdrv_defer_flush_to_disk(false);
     cpu_enable_ticks();
     runstate_set(state);
     vm_state_notify(1, state);
@@ -553,6 +568,10 @@ int vm_stop_force_state(RunState state)
         runstate_set(state);
 
         bdrv_drain_all();
+        /* As in do_vm_stop() */
+        if (state == RUN_STATE_FINISH_MIGRATE && migrate_defer_disk_flush()) {
+            bdrv_defer_flush_to_disk(true);
+        }
         /*
          * Make sure to return an error if the flush in a previous vm_stop()
          * failed.
